          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em convex function
            is a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            defined on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex set
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            is the boundary of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+set"} convex set
          %p
            There is another context where people say a function is convex if it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lipschitz+function"} Lipschitz function
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            with Lipschitz constant (or Lipschitz modulus) 1. These are different concepts of convexity, although there are relations between convexity and Lipschitz continuity, as we shall see below.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon D \to \mathbb{R}
            is
            %strong convex
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo :
                  %mi z
                  %mo ≥
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(x, z) \in D \times \mathbb{R}: z \geq f(x)\}
            is a convex subspace of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \times \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %strong convex
            if for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in D
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi t
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(t x + (1-t) y) \leq t f(x) + (1-t) f(y)
          %p
            whenever
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi t
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq t \leq 1
          %p
            This definition obviously extends to functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon D \to I
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            (whether open or closed or half-open, it doesn’t matter).
          %p
            The function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is called
            %strong concave
            if it satisfy the reverse inequality to the one given above, or equivalently if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -f
            is convex.
          %p
            A function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %strong strictly convex
            if the inequality holds strictly whenever
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi t
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt t \lt 1
            %em concave upward
            for strictly convex and
            %em concave downward
            for strictly concave.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+sets"} convex sets
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \to \mathbb{R}
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
                function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{R}
                is convex. This follows readily from multiplicativity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|x y|} = {|x|} \cdot {|y|}
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"} triangle inequality
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ≤
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|x + y|} \leq {|x|} + {|y|}
            %li
              %p
                More generally, for a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+space"} normed vector space
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|(-)\|}
                is convex, again by the triangle inequality and the scaling axiom
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi α
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|\alpha v\|} = {|\alpha|} \cdot {\|v\|}
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalars"} scalars
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            %li
              %p
                For any twice-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+function"} differentiable function
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon (a, b) \to \mathbb{R}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ″
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f''
                is nonnegative iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is convex; this may be proven using the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mean+value+theorem"} mean value theorem
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+function"} exponential function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp: (-\infty, \infty) \to \mathbb{R}
                and the
                = succeed "-power" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo :
                      %mi t
                      %mo ↦
                      %msup
                        %mi t
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, \infty) \to \mathbb{R}: t \mapsto t^p
                if
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \geq 1
            %li
              %p
                More generally, for an open convex region
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n
                in a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: D \to \mathbb{R}
                is convex iff its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hessian"} Hessian
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidefinite+element"} positive semidefinite
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+form"} bilinear form
            %li
              %p
                Any positive
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combination"} linear combination
                of convex functions on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is again convex.
            %li
              %p
                The pointwise
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximum"} maximum
                of two convex functions on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is again convex.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: V \to W
                is a homomorphism or convex-linear map between
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+spaces"} convex spaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi W
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: W \to \mathbb{R}
                is convex, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ g: V \to \mathbb{R}
                is convex.
          %p
            In the next two examples,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \subseteq \mathbb{R}
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                It is not generally true that a composition
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi g
                      %mi I
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi f
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \stackrel{g}{\to} I \stackrel{f}{\to} \mathbb{R}
                of convex functions is convex. For example, this fails for the case
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = \mathbb{R}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(x) = x^2 + 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: [1, \infty) \to \mathbb{R}
                given by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = x^{-1}
            %li
              %p
                However, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: I \to \mathbb{R}
                is both
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monotone+function"} monotone increasing
                and convex, then for any convex function
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo :
                        %mi D
                        %mo →
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: D \to I
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ g: D \to \mathbb{R}
                is convex (as is easily shown).
          %p
            A special case of the last class of examples are functions of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^f = \exp \circ f
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is convex. We say a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: D \to (0, \infty)
            is
            %strong log-convex
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi log
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log f
            is convex. We see then that log-convex functions are also convex. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            is an example of a convex function that is
            %em not
            log-convex (or use
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto x^2
            for a strict example).
          %h2#properties Properties
          #squeeze.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: (a, b) \to \mathbb{R}
              is convex and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi v
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lt v \lt w \in (a, b)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo −
                        %mi v
                    %mo ≤
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo −
                        %mi w
                    %mo ≤
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo −
                        %mi w
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{f(u) - f(v)}{u - v} \leq \frac{f(u) - f(w)}{u - w} \leq \frac{f(v) - f(w)}{v - w}.
            %p
              Consequently, the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto \frac{f(x) - f(v)}{x - v}
              on the domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lt x \lt v
              is increasing and is bounded above by
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo −
                          %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{f(v)-f(w)}{v-w}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \lt x \lt w
              is increasing and bounded below by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi u
                          %mo −
                          %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{f(u)-f(v)}{u-v}
          %p
            The proof is virtually trivial; just write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            as a convex combination
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mi u
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t u + (1-t)w
            and use the definition of convexity.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A convex function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: (a, b) \to \mathbb{R}
              is continuous.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For any point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0 \in (a, b)
              there are
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s, t, u, v \in (a, b)
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi t
                      %mo &lt;
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi u
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \lt t \lt x_0 \lt u \lt v
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in (t, x_0) \cup (x_0, u)
              we have by Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#squeeze"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                    %mo ≤
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo −
                        %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{f(s)-f(t)}{s-t} \leq \frac{f(x) - f(x_0)}{x-x_0} \leq \frac{f(u)-f(v)}{u-v}
            %p
              so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %mi max
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi s
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo −
                          %mi t
                      %mo |
                    %mo ,
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi u
                          %mo −
                          %mi v
                      %mo |
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = \max\{\left\vert \frac{f(s)-f(t)}{s-t}\right\vert, \left\vert \frac{f(u)-f(v)}{u-v}\right\vert\}
              serves as a Lipschitz constant, i.e., we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |f(x) - f(x_0)| \leq K|x - x_0|
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo ,
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in (t, u)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
          %p In the converse direction, we have the following result which frequently arises in practice.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n
              is a convex set and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: D \to \mathbb{R}
              is a continuous function such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mi y
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\left(\frac{x+y}{2}\right) \leq \frac{f(x) + f(y)}{2},
            %p
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is convex.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              For any fixed
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h: [0, 1] \to \mathbb{R}
              defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(t) = t f(x) + (1-t)f(y) - f(t x + (1-t)y)
            %p
              is continuous. The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^{-1}([0, \infty))
              is closed in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, 1]
              and, by an easy induction argument, contains the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dyadic+rational+numbers"} dyadic rational numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0, 1]
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, 1]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi h
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^{-1}([0, \infty))
              is all of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, 1]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(t) \geq 0
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0, 1]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is convex.
          %p
            Another easy consequence of Lemma
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#squeeze"}
            is
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For a convex function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: (a, b) \to \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ↘
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ↗
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{x \searrow x_0}{\lim} \frac{f(x)-f(x_0)}{x-x_0}, \qquad \underset{x \nearrow x_0}{\lim} \frac{f(x)-f(x_0)}{x-x_0}
            %p
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              exist at every point
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0 \in (a, b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
              is less than or equal to the right-hand derivative at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
          %p
            It further follows from Lemma
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#squeeze"}
            that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is convex and we define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D f)(x_0)
            to be the average of the right-hand and left-hand derivatives, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D f
            is monotone increasing and hence is discontinuous at at most countable many points of jump discontinuity (whence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D f
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+integration"} Riemann-integrable
